; Template for the local BIND 9 CI gate's srp.test. zone (plan S14 Option C). start_bind9
; copies this into the scratch runtime directory before starting named -- BIND rewrites its
; own working copy (SOA serial bumps, dynamic-update journal replay) so the source tree's
; copy must never be the one actually served.
;
; The apex KEY is the SRP test keystore's own key (tests/keystore-srp-bind9/), granted
; zonesub update rights in named.conf.in -- the proxy signs every forwarded UPDATE with this
; same key (handlers.srp_handler's keystore_dir points at that directory in test_srp.sh, and
; in test_update.sh's local mode, which runs srp_handler here alongside the RFC 9664 handler
; on update.test.).
$TTL 3600
@       IN SOA  ns.srp.test. admin.srp.test. ( 1 3600 900 604800 3600 )
        IN NS   ns.srp.test.
ns      IN A    127.0.0.1
@       IN KEY  512 3 15 FNZq5ao1LH+zGRNOz0yeZvMVjlSwG+OYRCpz33kdeBg=

; RFC 9665 S3.1.1 discovery: srp.test. is the zone apex, so a requester finds its registrar
; by an SRV lookup for this name, then an address lookup for the target. test_srp.sh's
; discovery test does exactly that (no -server). start_bind9 replaces @SRP_REGISTRAR_PORT@
; with BIND9_SRP_REGISTRAR_PORT, which test_srp.sh sets to the port its proxy listens on.
_dnssd-srp._tcp IN SRV 0 0 @SRP_REGISTRAR_PORT@ proxy.srp.test.
; A requester that uses TLS looks up _dnssd-srp-tls._tcp instead (RFC 9665 S3.1.1, S7): it
; points at the proxy's DNS-over-TLS listener, which test_srp.sh's TLS discovery test finds
; and sends to. start_bind9 replaces @SRP_REGISTRAR_TLS_PORT@ with
; BIND9_SRP_REGISTRAR_TLS_PORT, which test_srp.sh sets to that listener's port.
_dnssd-srp-tls._tcp IN SRV 0 0 @SRP_REGISTRAR_TLS_PORT@ proxy.srp.test.
proxy   IN A    127.0.0.1

; Non-SRP data at a name with no KEY: test_srp.sh's foreign-data takeover test claims this
; name with refuse_on_foreign_data: false, which makes the proxy forward a "KEY RRset does
; not exist" prerequisite (RFC 2136 S2.4.3) that BIND must accept.
legacy  IN A    192.0.2.99
